{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they heard.</b> There are many aggadah midrashim, and our Rabbis have already arranged them in their proper place in Bereshit Rabbah and in other midrash collections; but I come only for the plain sense of Scripture and for the aggadah that settles the words of Scripture, each word according to its context. <b>And they heard.</b> What did they hear? They heard the voice of the Holy One, blessed be He, as He was walking in the garden." "<b>To the wind of the day.</b> To that wind toward which the sun comes — and that is westward; for toward evening the sun is in the west, and they sinned in the tenth hour (Sanhedrin 38)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:21.897934808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}